Zipcar revolutionized urban mobility since 2000 by enabling members to reserve and access shared vehicles for as little as 30 minutes through mobile apps. Each Zipcar removes approximately 21 privately owned vehicles from city streets; members own nearly 80% fewer vehicles than average households. The business model demonstrates use-oriented services where ownership shifts to access, reducing consumption while maintaining utility. Members save approximately $1,000 monthly compared to car ownership. Zipcar's partnerships with underserved communities, including housing authorities and zero-emissions mobility programs, showcase how collaborative consumption can address equity while reducing urban congestion and carbon emissions.